{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"929377169382ef94fc9269f7b427e160a7f1389beabc8063e166afe4fd74a0d3","digest":{"component_or_area":"bedrock LLM provider, review-bot service","key_entities":["REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","boto3.session.Session().region_name","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py::build_bedrock_provider","BedrockProvider","tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","review-bot service","LLMConfigError"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock","region configuration","llm provider","no region error","review bot"],"propositions":["review-bot container lacks AWS region configuration, causing boto3 client construction to fail with NoRegionError before any Bedrock call","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION is unset in the container environment and build_bedrock_provider passes None to boto3, which cannot resolve region from IMDS or ambient sources","boto3 resolves region from AWS_DEFAULT_REGION (not AWS_REGION) and this configuration is missing from the container","pydantic-ai raises UserError on missing region, which is not caught by rebar's LLMError handlers, leaving the review gate unprotected","CloudWatch voter metrics in review-bot fail silently for the same missing-region reason, breaking rollback-plan alarm dependency"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787678306955753001,"uuid":"94214d67-fca3-43e0-9e33-8bf8b101f7a6"}